WEBVTT

00:19.750 --> 00:21.550
This is incredible!

00:21.550 --> 00:24.170
Synthesizing adamantite alloy...

00:24.170 --> 00:26.550
with such a complex alchemy circle...

00:26.970 --> 00:33.490
Still, the fundamental structure is the 
same as the circle for spiraling sweets.

00:33.490 --> 00:36.060
Ah! I'll do that!

00:36.060 --> 00:41.010
You'll be able to create alchemy circles 
like that soon enough, Reyva.

00:42.140 --> 00:44.110
You think I will?

00:44.110 --> 00:45.980
They're so advanced...

00:45.980 --> 00:47.360
Of course you will.

00:47.360 --> 00:53.530
After all, you possesses the most 
important quality an alchemist needs.

00:53.530 --> 00:55.180
What's that?

00:55.570 --> 00:59.900
Your eyes shine with excitement as you watch 
the process of things coming together.

01:00.150 --> 01:03.880
Yes! It's so, <i>so</i> fascinating!

01:03.880 --> 01:06.540
Alright, then I think I'll have you help

01:06.540 --> 01:09.130
actually synthesize some of 
the simple components next.

01:09.130 --> 01:11.290
Yes! I'll do it!

02:43.300 --> 02:47.930
<b>Episode 8
Let's Choose a Party Name!</b>

02:43.300 --> 02:47.930
<b>Episode 8
Let's Choose a Party Name!</b>

02:48.180 --> 02:52.190
<b>Day of Takumi's Audience with the King of Barcula</b>

02:49.630 --> 02:52.960
Oh? Is this your carriage?

02:52.960 --> 02:54.350
Oh, no.

02:54.350 --> 02:57.030
It's a carriage being presented 
to His Royal Majesty.

02:57.030 --> 02:58.870
I just made it.

02:58.870 --> 03:00.310
You <i>made</i> it?

03:00.310 --> 03:01.340
<i>You</i> did?

03:01.340 --> 03:02.350
Yes.

03:02.350 --> 03:06.540
Hm, you're even better than 
I've heard, Sir Takumi Iruma.

03:06.540 --> 03:09.130
Huh? How do you know my name?

03:09.130 --> 03:11.500
Y-Your Majesty!

03:11.500 --> 03:12.460
"Your Majesty"?

03:13.120 --> 03:15.490
My apologies for the late introduction.

03:15.490 --> 03:18.790
I'm the man who rules this 
kingdom, Lobos Barcula.

03:18.790 --> 03:22.450
Y-You're the <i>king?!</i>

03:23.470 --> 03:26.040
No need to be so formal, Mr. Iruma.

03:26.040 --> 03:28.430
This is an unofficial audience.

03:28.430 --> 03:32.890
I-I thought we would be having the 
audience in the reception room!

03:32.890 --> 03:35.150
Is there some deeper meaning for this?

03:35.150 --> 03:36.400
Of course.

03:37.180 --> 03:41.700
Making you all wait in a stuffy room 
for a personal audience with me,

03:41.700 --> 03:46.110
only for me to show up with an
 ostentatious procession of subordinates

03:46.110 --> 03:49.110
would be overly formal and dull!

03:50.430 --> 03:53.070
Well, setting that joke aside.

03:53.340 --> 03:58.290
I wanted to meet this famous alchemist and 
thank him without standing on formality.

03:58.290 --> 04:00.250
Th-Thank me?

04:00.250 --> 04:01.650
Mr. Iruma.

04:01.650 --> 04:05.430
Thanks to you, the royal capital has 
a resolution to its sewage problem.

04:05.430 --> 04:06.370
You have my thanks.

04:06.370 --> 04:09.460
N-Not at all! Y-You don't need to bow 
your head to me, Your Majesty!

04:10.070 --> 04:13.300
Normally, I would host a grand banquet

04:13.300 --> 04:16.190
and bestow lavish rewards 
and a peerage upon you,

04:16.590 --> 04:19.990
but that would invite the risk 
of unwanted interference.

04:19.990 --> 04:21.110
Forgive me.

04:21.110 --> 04:27.400
No, I'm grateful to you for keeping 
me out of Sidonia's firing line.

04:27.920 --> 04:32.400
Protecting the people is my duty as king.

04:32.890 --> 04:34.370
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

04:34.370 --> 04:39.090
<i>It seems like, just like the lord,
the king doesn't stand on airs.</i>

04:42.870 --> 04:47.980
<i>The king gave me a reward for the magical 
devices that resolved their sewage problem,</i>

04:47.980 --> 04:50.350
<i>and then we left the castle.</i>

04:52.230 --> 04:54.370
Simon, Galahat.

04:54.370 --> 04:57.530
I never met with anyone today.

04:57.530 --> 04:58.430
Understood?

04:58.430 --> 04:59.280
Yes.

04:59.280 --> 05:01.690
I'll place a gag order on 
those within the castle.

05:01.920 --> 05:05.570
However, once we export those 
magical devices to other nations,

05:05.570 --> 05:09.350
Iruma's influence will 
only spread even further.

05:09.350 --> 05:12.500
That's precisely what I'm concerned about.

05:13.050 --> 05:17.390
Once that happens, the Church of
Divine Light is certain to act.

05:19.850 --> 05:22.560
<i>Several days after we returned to 
Bolton from the royal capital,</i>

05:23.300 --> 05:28.620
<i>I officially purchased the mansion 
I was renting through the Papek Company.</i>

05:31.960 --> 05:35.900
It's my... <i>our</i> home now.

05:38.920 --> 05:42.150
Huh? You don't want any wages again?

05:42.150 --> 05:45.430
You provide us with plenty for food already,

05:45.430 --> 05:48.920
so I'm happy with just the 
usual allowance you give me.

05:48.920 --> 05:51.130
I don't really need it either.

05:51.360 --> 05:54.170
Still, even if you don't need it now,

05:54.170 --> 06:00.080
wouldn't it be good to build up savings 
for the day your contract with me ends?

06:00.290 --> 06:04.870
As an elf, I'll probably long outlive you.

06:04.870 --> 06:09.550
So I'll spend my remaining 
days protecting your grave.

06:09.550 --> 06:10.340
Huh?

06:10.340 --> 06:14.250
If I could live just one 
day longer than you,

06:14.250 --> 06:18.990
and then have my grave placed next 
to yours, that would be perfect!

06:21.440 --> 06:23.900
<b>The Holy Empire of Sidonia</b>

06:21.890 --> 06:23.510
I see.

06:23.890 --> 06:28.000
So this is the magic device being 
used to purify sewage in Bolton.

06:28.360 --> 06:33.450
Yes. We infiltrated Bakilatos and 
managed to obtain just the one.

06:33.450 --> 06:36.820
What an abhorrently heretical magical device.

06:37.330 --> 06:40.490
They act without any fear of Anat's anger.

06:40.490 --> 06:43.550
Father, Pope Walbarr, has 
deeply lamented this as well.

06:43.950 --> 06:45.940
Within the Church of Divine Light,

06:45.940 --> 06:50.510
there are those who say we should decisively
 strike down the source of this evil immediately.

06:50.510 --> 06:53.250
You mean the Divine Light Squadron, I believe.

06:53.250 --> 06:53.980
Yes.

06:54.560 --> 06:57.000
The source of this evil resides in Bolton.

06:57.440 --> 07:01.480
We will not tolerate those who threaten 
the dignity of our Pope and Anat.

07:01.770 --> 07:05.690
It wouldn't hurt to quickly 
nip this disaster in the bud.

07:06.060 --> 07:09.290
May all be as the great Anat wills it.

07:11.760 --> 07:14.110
Register with the Adventurer's Guild?

07:14.110 --> 07:15.040
Yes.

07:15.040 --> 07:19.590
I'd like to help as an adventurer 
too, like Sofia and Maria do.

07:19.590 --> 07:23.920
In order to help you as an 
alchemist and a craftsman,

07:23.920 --> 07:27.290
I want to raise my stats and 
increase my mana even more!

07:27.560 --> 07:28.950
I see.

07:28.950 --> 07:32.490
I guess it's true that adventuring 
is a good way to increase your mana.

07:32.490 --> 07:33.300
Yeah.

07:34.570 --> 07:37.220
Here's your registration card, Reyva.

07:37.220 --> 07:39.400
Thank you so much!

07:39.400 --> 07:45.180
I'm grateful that you're willing to send 
my money home for a low fee as well!

07:45.180 --> 07:48.340
There are actually plenty of 
adventurers like you who ask us

07:48.340 --> 07:50.380
to send money to their families.

07:50.650 --> 07:52.310
It's easy enough to handle.

07:52.310 --> 07:53.600
That's a big help.

07:53.600 --> 07:55.670
By the way, Takumi,

07:55.670 --> 07:58.740
would you name your party already?

07:58.740 --> 08:00.070
Name our party?

08:00.270 --> 08:03.050
Everyone but Reyva is rank D.

08:03.050 --> 08:08.550
Though, to be blunt, yours is one 
of the top-class parties at our guild.

08:08.550 --> 08:10.830
You can't remain nameless forever.

08:10.830 --> 08:14.830
A party name... 
You mean like the Lion's Fang?

08:14.830 --> 08:15.510
Yeah.

08:15.510 --> 08:19.510
Hm, but I've never set 
out to be an adventurer.

08:19.510 --> 08:23.630
Besides, we don't have clear role divisions 
like the three in the Lion's Fang.

08:23.630 --> 08:26.730
We don't have a front-liner, 
plain and simple.

08:26.730 --> 08:30.200
It might be better if I could fight 
a little further in the front.

08:30.200 --> 08:31.870
Leave that to me!

08:32.930 --> 08:34.080
Barack?!

08:34.080 --> 08:35.910
He's huge!

08:35.910 --> 08:37.950
An adventurer's body is their biggest asset!

08:37.950 --> 08:40.910
If you have a strong body, then you 
can survive anything that happens!

08:40.910 --> 08:42.830
Did you hear what I said?

08:42.830 --> 08:45.280
I'm not aiming to be an adventurer—

08:45.280 --> 08:46.490
I'll train you!

08:49.650 --> 08:51.510
Get back on your feet!

08:52.970 --> 08:57.480
Hans told you to come up 
with a party name, right?!

08:58.110 --> 08:59.950
Have you thought of anything?!

08:59.950 --> 09:03.530
I-I've thought of something!

09:03.530 --> 09:05.550
What name are you considering?!

09:05.550 --> 09:08.270
W-We're Adventurers.

09:08.270 --> 09:11.250
What the hell?! Rejected!

09:11.250 --> 09:13.690
Ow!

09:14.250 --> 09:18.170
What symbolizes the Takumi Iruma 
who was born into this world?!

09:18.410 --> 09:21.120
Now, spit it out!
Say your party name!

09:21.120 --> 09:23.580
F-Father of Toilets.

09:23.580 --> 09:25.840
Are you takin' this seriously?!

09:26.030 --> 09:29.610
Pick something snappier, like the Lion's Fang!

09:29.610 --> 09:31.130
The Toilet Lid!

09:31.130 --> 09:33.500
Get your mind off of the toilets!

09:33.500 --> 09:35.920
The path to being an alchemist...

09:35.920 --> 09:38.130
is a thorny one.

09:39.860 --> 09:42.150
Our party name?

09:42.150 --> 09:45.690
Yeah. Can you think of a good one?

09:45.690 --> 09:50.170
He throws me around every time he rejects
 a name, and my body won't last at this rate.

09:51.160 --> 09:54.390
How about "Mr. Takumi and His Servants"?

09:54.690 --> 09:59.110
I'll probably get thrown around for 
ones that are short descriptions.

09:59.110 --> 10:00.270
I know!

10:00.270 --> 10:05.040
How about "An Adventurer Mastering Alchemy, 
His Bodyguard, His Maid,

10:05.040 --> 10:09.600
His Pets, and an 
Alchemist-In-Training"?

10:09.600 --> 10:13.040
That's a detailed description, 
but it's awfully long.

10:13.040 --> 10:17.600
He told me to come up with one that 
better represents who we are.

10:18.260 --> 10:21.370
"Toilets, Refrigerators, 
Underwear, and Mr. Takumi"?

10:21.370 --> 10:23.940
I'd probably get thrown four 
or five times for that one.

10:25.210 --> 10:30.170
I-I can't believe I came up with a name that 
would get you get thrown four or five times!

10:30.170 --> 10:35.550
I'm just a walking toilet with a sign 
reading "I'll handle the housework!"—

10:31.940 --> 10:38.400
<b>"I'll Handle
the Housework"</b>

10:35.550 --> 10:38.400
no, even lower than that!

10:39.240 --> 10:41.150
U-Um, Maria...

10:41.150 --> 10:45.230
Barack also told me to get 
my mind off of toilets.

10:45.230 --> 10:48.400
Coming up with a name is hard, isn't it?

10:48.400 --> 10:50.120
Do you have any ideas, Sofia?

10:50.120 --> 10:51.750
How dare he!

10:51.750 --> 10:54.070
Leaving Mr. Takumi this ragged!

10:54.440 --> 10:57.290
How dare he, how dare he,
how <i>dare</i> he!

10:57.290 --> 10:59.250
S-Sofia?!

10:59.250 --> 11:02.640
I'm heading out now to go 
cut that large man down!

11:02.640 --> 11:04.520
Wait, wait!

11:04.520 --> 11:06.270
He's just training me! That's all!

11:06.270 --> 11:07.190
But!

