Earth Magic Lv8, Ice Magic Lv5,
Lightning Magic Lv5,
Space-Time Magic Lv6,
Enchanting Lv8, Alchemy Lv9,
Blacksmithing Lv9, Woodworking Lv8,
Carpentry Lv5, Gathering Lv6,
Logging Lv5, Butchering Lv4,
Mining Lv4, Metalworking Lv8,
Sewing Lv7, Cooking Lv2</b>

11:07.410 --> 11:10.530
It's true that, thanks to him,
I managed to level up

11:10.530 --> 11:15.890
my Intuition, Evasion, Body Control, 
and Martial Arts skills today.

11:18.350 --> 11:22.250
<i>It looks like I'm going to suffer 
until we decide on a name.</i>

11:23.990 --> 11:27.450
<b>The Holy Empire of Sidonia
Ten Months After Takumi's Present Time</b>

11:33.330 --> 11:34.800
Come on! What's wrong?

11:34.800 --> 11:36.360
Holding back again?

11:36.360 --> 11:37.750
I don't need that anymore!

11:40.530 --> 11:43.150
He just keeps charging 
in without pulling back.

11:43.150 --> 11:45.470
That won't work in real combat.

11:45.470 --> 11:47.600
And your style would?

11:47.600 --> 11:49.380
<i>I'm</i> a hero.

11:49.380 --> 11:52.140
Yamato and I are both called that as well.

11:52.520 --> 11:55.980
More importantly, why don't we ditch 
this and go somewhere together?

11:55.980 --> 11:56.600
No, thanks.

11:56.780 --> 11:58.160
What?

11:58.160 --> 12:01.610
Are you worried about your 
slave attendant watching?

12:01.610 --> 12:06.480
Hey now, you're acting the same 
as before we were summoned.

12:07.220 --> 12:09.590
<i>You were less bad back then.</i>

12:17.150 --> 12:22.350
<i>"Anat created mankind, and then created 
the beastmen and elves to serve them."</i>

12:22.660 --> 12:26.580
<i>The Church of Divine Light preaches 
absolute human supremacy.</i>

12:26.580 --> 12:32.260
<i>Based on what I heard the other day 
from merchants traveling between nations,</i>

12:32.260 --> 12:37.250
<i>the Church of Creation teaches that 
"all races are children of Nolyn."</i>

12:38.050 --> 12:43.450
<i>This nation dominated by the Church of 
Divine Light summoned us, so what is our role...</i>

12:45.270 --> 12:46.570
<i>supposed to be?</i>

12:47.910 --> 12:50.320
<i>They tell us we're here for world peace,</i>

12:50.870 --> 12:52.920
<i>but what are they trying to make us do?</i>

12:54.150 --> 12:55.110
Here.

12:55.580 --> 12:58.250
Are these for me?

12:58.530 --> 13:02.960
It's a ring for activating spells, 
and you said you could use a staff,

13:02.960 --> 13:05.000
so I made you one from an Elder Treant.

13:05.500 --> 13:08.460
The metal wrapped around 
it is a mythril alloy.

13:08.900 --> 13:12.100
You'll need good equipment 
when we go adventuring.

13:12.100 --> 13:13.670
Thank you very much!

13:14.050 --> 13:17.360
Lucky, getting weapons.

13:17.360 --> 13:18.840
This is for you, Maple.

13:18.840 --> 13:21.140
A-A weapon for <i>me?!</i>

13:21.140 --> 13:25.950
I figured you'd need one that wouldn't get in
the way when you manipulate your threads.

13:25.950 --> 13:28.110
I had Reyva help me make it.

13:28.110 --> 13:31.760
Thank you, Master! Reyva!

13:33.890 --> 13:35.280
The Cat's Claw!

13:36.230 --> 13:38.490
Stop focusing on the Lion's Fang!

13:38.490 --> 13:39.900
Mr. Takumi!

13:39.900 --> 13:44.710
How about "Crush That Big Man, 
Mr. Takumi and His Servants"?

13:45.320 --> 13:46.680
Ow!

13:45.750 --> 13:46.680
Rejected!

13:46.940 --> 13:48.050
<i>This is bad.</i>

13:48.050 --> 13:50.950
<i>At this rate, Sofia might snap.</i>

13:51.380 --> 13:54.090
Mr. Takumi, your defense is too lax!

13:54.090 --> 13:54.860
Huh?

13:54.860 --> 13:56.440
You have too many openings!

13:56.440 --> 13:57.820
React faster!

13:57.820 --> 14:02.550
The Guild Master's attacks are aimed 
precisely at your weak spots!

14:02.550 --> 14:04.670
<i>She's turned instructor on me.</i>

14:05.400 --> 14:08.730
Takumi, are you interested in 
taking on an escort quest?

14:08.730 --> 14:10.700
Oh, good idea.

14:10.700 --> 14:12.960
If you succeed, you'll rank up.

14:12.960 --> 14:16.420
Escort? How many days would it take?

14:16.640 --> 14:22.890
Well, with your carriage, it'll only take 
four days to go the town of Kilbus and back.

14:23.210 --> 14:25.820
The request comes from the Papek Company.

14:25.820 --> 14:29.330
Don't the three from the Lion's Fang
usually take the escort quests?

14:29.330 --> 14:33.820
Unfortunately, the Lion's Fang is 
already out on a different quest.

14:34.250 --> 14:38.740
Serving as the Lion's Fang's
 backup is a heavy responsibility.

14:42.270 --> 14:44.070
We'll accept the quest.

14:44.370 --> 14:48.020
Come up with your party name 
by the time you return, okay?

14:50.740 --> 14:53.710
Yahoo!

14:52.150 --> 14:54.080
Come on, monsters!

14:54.080 --> 14:56.190
Bring it if you can!

14:57.290 --> 15:01.120
It's reassuring to have you all as my escort.

15:01.120 --> 15:04.830
It would be nice if there 
weren't any monster attacks.

15:05.100 --> 15:09.290
We've packed up many daily necessities in 
addition to the purification magical devices.

15:09.690 --> 15:14.130
Our president asked me to 
purchase milk while I'm there, too.

15:14.130 --> 15:16.260
Huh? They have milk there?

15:16.260 --> 15:20.000
Yes, though it doesn't 
reach Bolton very often.

15:20.000 --> 15:22.630
They also have other dairy products.

15:22.630 --> 15:26.820
Uh, it was... oh, yes, cheese.

15:26.820 --> 15:28.030
Cheese?!

15:28.460 --> 15:31.040
<i>They have milk </i>and<i> cheese!</i>

15:35.900 --> 15:37.180
Monsters?

15:45.470 --> 15:48.710
It looks like a territorial conflict 
between Goblins and Bush Wolves.

15:48.710 --> 15:51.520
Camellia, go!

16:01.100 --> 16:03.340
Dead in an instant, huh?

16:03.340 --> 16:07.930
I doubt there are monsters willing 
to attack this caravan.

16:09.100 --> 16:11.490
They were all bark, no bite!

16:12.490 --> 16:14.950
<b>Town of Kilbus</b>

16:17.520 --> 16:19.620
<i>It's cream stew!</i>

16:19.620 --> 16:22.710
It's a white soup? How curious!

16:22.710 --> 16:24.580
It has a nice smell, though!

16:24.580 --> 16:26.870
Time to dig in!

16:31.290 --> 16:33.010
Tasty!

16:33.290 --> 16:36.730
<i>Yeah, there are plenty of 
points to improve on,</i>

16:37.230 --> 16:38.780
<i>but it's a nostalgic taste.</i>

16:40.710 --> 16:42.140
Mr. Takumi?

16:42.470 --> 16:45.960
We need to buy milk and 
cheese before we go home.

16:45.960 --> 16:49.110
I hear the market is open 
at night in this town.

16:49.460 --> 16:50.330
Good.

16:54.570 --> 16:56.110
So good!

16:56.110 --> 16:59.270
It's my first time eating cheese.

16:59.270 --> 17:02.750
I wish I could let my mother and 
little brother taste this, too.

17:03.740 --> 17:07.160
<i>It's only been a few months 
since I came to this world,</i>

17:07.910 --> 17:11.170
<i>and yet it feels like 
it's already been years.</i>

17:12.100 --> 17:15.730
<i>I'll never go back to my old life.</i>

17:15.730 --> 17:18.380
<i>I'm in another world.</i>

17:18.880 --> 17:22.360
<i>Having thoughts like that must 
be due to the milk and cheese</i>

17:22.360 --> 17:25.360
<i>making me nostalgic for my old world.</i>

17:26.730 --> 17:28.330
No way there's rice?

17:28.880 --> 17:31.020
There's no rice here, right?

17:31.340 --> 17:35.480
Are you referring to the grain they 
eat in the Kingdom of Samandor?

17:35.860 --> 17:38.040
They have rice?!

17:38.040 --> 17:40.620
It isn't on the market in Barcula though.

17:40.620 --> 17:43.130
I think they were selling 
it in the royal capital.

17:43.130 --> 17:46.250
No way!

17:44.450 --> 17:48.660
<i>If I'd known, I would have 
peeked in at the market!</i>

17:48.660 --> 17:51.560
You want to eat rice that badly?

17:51.560 --> 17:53.640
Well, of course.

17:53.980 --> 17:57.980
I-I've heard rumors, 
so I wanted to try it.

17:59.600 --> 18:03.180
Mr. Takumi? Did something happen?

18:03.620 --> 18:05.070
Hey, Sofia...

18:05.070 --> 18:08.470
It's been over a decade since 
you left your hometown, right?

18:08.470 --> 18:09.810
Huh? Yes.

18:10.100 --> 18:11.450
Do you ever...

18:11.450 --> 18:14.280
get nostalgic for your hometown, 
or your hometown's food?

18:14.690 --> 18:16.980
Do you ever want to go back?

18:17.230 --> 18:21.450
I enjoy the present a lot more than 
reminiscing over my hometown.

18:21.450 --> 18:23.380
For nearly 50 years,

18:23.380 --> 18:28.150
I lived under that curse 
like a caged bird.

18:28.150 --> 18:33.120
But forming a contract with you 
has allowed me to live a new life.

18:34.130 --> 18:37.580
I wonder what kind of experiences 
await me with everyone here,

18:37.580 --> 18:39.950
and moving forward with you all

18:40.490 --> 18:41.700
feels wonderful

18:42.140 --> 18:43.320
and precious.

18:43.930 --> 18:48.560
Mr. Takumi, you gave me 
wings when I was caged.

18:49.390 --> 18:51.010
Wings?

18:51.010 --> 18:55.480
Time had stopped for me, but you gave me 
the wings to take flight and move forward.

18:55.480 --> 18:57.160
So now...

18:57.160 --> 19:00.700
I only look at the life that 
awaits me in the future.

19:01.010 --> 19:04.150
There's no need for me to 
look back on old times.

19:04.440 --> 19:10.570
Every day I find myself more excited 
for today and the day after, too!

19:10.570 --> 19:12.320
Me, too!

19:12.320 --> 19:13.610
Me, too!

19:14.390 --> 19:15.830
Camellia says her, too!

19:16.350 --> 19:17.530
I see.

19:17.980 --> 19:21.200
<i>I've started living a new life as well.</i>

19:22.000 --> 19:25.870
<i>I guess you could say
 I've been given wings.</i>

19:26.390 --> 19:28.510
<i>Though the one who gave 
me those wings was...</i>

19:31.960 --> 19:33.390
Wings...

19:33.390 --> 19:36.180
How about the "Wings of Nolyn"?

19:36.790 --> 19:38.400
The Wings of Nolyn?

19:38.400 --> 19:40.090
For our party name?

19:40.090 --> 19:40.660
Yeah.

19:40.950 --> 19:45.360
I think we've given each other wings.

19:45.360 --> 19:47.300
Which is why we're able to move forward.

19:48.160 --> 19:49.650
The Wings of Nolyn.

19:49.650 --> 19:50.580
I like it.

19:50.580 --> 19:52.300
It's cool!

19:52.300 --> 19:54.000
I'm all for it!

19:54.000 --> 19:55.970
No objections here!

19:56.480 --> 19:57.670
Then it's settled!

19:57.670 --> 19:59.420
Our party name will be...

19:59.820 --> 20:01.670
The Wings of Nolyn!

20:03.570 --> 20:07.600
<i>After safely completed our escort 
quest, we returned to Bolton</i>

20:07.600 --> 20:09.290
<i>two nights later.</i>

20:16.690 --> 20:18.190
<i>Paralysis poison?!</i>

20:18.190 --> 20:19.800
<i>There's poison mist filling the mansion!</i>

20:19.800 --> 20:20.910
Don't move.

20:24.120 --> 20:26.810
Mr. Takumi!

20:33.520 --> 20:34.410
Wha?!

20:36.490 --> 20:37.950
Why, you!

20:45.040 --> 20:45.960
Phew.

20:45.960 --> 20:46.820
Thank you.

20:46.820 --> 20:48.510
You saved us, Maple.

20:48.820 --> 20:49.970
Cure.

20:57.000 --> 20:59.400
The numbness is all gone?

20:59.930 --> 21:02.980
Mr. Takumi! I'm so sorry!

21:02.980 --> 21:04.290
I've let you down!

21:04.640 --> 21:06.350
It wasn't your fault, Sofia.

21:06.350 --> 21:09.830
Why weren't you paralyzed, Mr. Takumi?

21:10.210 --> 21:14.780
Maple and I both have the Poison Resistance 
and Paralysis Resistance skills.

21:14.780 --> 21:16.850
I did feel a little numb, though.

21:17.240 --> 21:20.930
Master, what do we do
with those outside?

21:21.760 --> 21:25.670
I found them wandering around when 
I led Camellia to her stable.

21:25.670 --> 21:28.090
I figured there might be some inside too,

21:28.090 --> 21:31.390
so I entered the pocket dimension, 
and then I saw everyone under attack.

21:31.640 --> 21:33.950
The assailants were well-armed.

21:33.950 --> 21:36.230
I think this attack was planned.

21:36.710 --> 21:41.120
It might be best to ask the 
Adventurer's Guild for assistance.

21:41.120 --> 21:41.900
Alright.

21:41.900 --> 21:46.130
Sofia, sorry to ask, but you could go 
to the Guild and fetch Barack for us?

21:53.510 --> 21:55.020
Takumi.

21:55.020 --> 21:58.480
I think you should report 
this to the lord at once.

21:58.920 --> 22:01.540
You think this is major trouble, too?

22:01.540 --> 22:02.780
Yeah.

22:02.780 --> 22:05.770
Most likely the worst kind there is.
